<?php

declare(strict_types=1);

// One source-readiness-bounded applied item per eligible specialization leaf.
// Each row is [difficulty, stem, answer, three distractors, explanation, source IDs].
return [
    'ece-authentic-assessment' => ['medium', 'A kindergarten teacher wants to understand whether a child can explain how a block structure works. Which evidence is most useful?', 'Observe the child explaining the structure during play and retain a brief work sample.', ['Use a timed worksheet that tests the same vocabulary without the structure.', 'Ask the family to estimate how often the child uses the target words at home.', 'Score the finished structure without asking how the child planned it.'], 'A focused observation and work sample connect the evidence to the intended language and reasoning in a natural context. A product alone may not show the child’s process or explanation.', ['deped-kindergarten-curriculum-guide-2023', 'prc-let-enhanced-tos-2025']],
    'ece-developmental-domains' => ['medium', 'During a group task, a child explains a plan, shares materials, and adjusts a hand movement to fit a small piece. What is the most useful interpretation?', 'The task gives evidence across language, social, cognitive, and motor development.', ['The child has advanced equally in every developmental domain.', 'The task should be scored only as a fine-motor activity.', 'The child’s sharing proves that no further social observation is needed.'], 'Real activities can engage several developmental domains at once, but one observation does not establish a complete developmental profile. Record the specific behaviors and contexts.', ['deped-kindergarten-curriculum-guide-2023', 'prc-let-enhanced-tos-2025']],
    'ece-developmental-observation' => ['easy', 'A teacher writes, “Mara was careless at centers,” after a child spills water while pouring. Which record would be more useful for later assessment?', 'Describe the materials, sequence, and child actions without assigning a trait.', ['Keep “careless” because it summarizes the teacher’s impression.', 'Record only that the center was untidy at the end of the activity.', 'Ask another adult whether the child is usually careless.'], 'An objective anecdotal record describes observable actions and context. A trait label obscures what happened and can bias later interpretation.', ['deped-kindergarten-curriculum-guide-2023', 'prc-let-enhanced-tos-2025']],
    'ece-emergent-literacy' => ['medium', 'A child dictates a story and invents spellings for several words. Which teacher response best supports emergent literacy?', 'Invite the child to reread the story and discuss how the written marks represent its words and ideas.', ['Replace the story with a copying sheet using only conventional spellings.', 'Correct every invented spelling before the child can share the story.', 'Delay writing activities until the child can spell each word conventionally.'], 'Emergent literacy develops through meaningful reading, writing, speaking, and print experiences. The teacher can extend the child’s understanding of print while preserving authorship and communication.', ['deped-kindergarten-curriculum-guide-2023', 'prc-let-enhanced-tos-2025']],
    'ece-family-partnership' => ['medium', 'A family explains that a child uses a home-language routine to settle before sleep, while the school observes difficulty during rest time. What is the best next step?', 'Discuss the family’s knowledge and jointly try a feasible routine, then review the child’s response.', ['Ask the family to stop the home routine so school practice stays uniform.', 'Adopt the home routine unchanged without checking school safety or feasibility.', 'Treat the difference as evidence that the family is not following school guidance.'], 'Partnership draws on family knowledge and school observations while planning a workable approach together. The team should observe the outcome and adjust with the family.', ['deped-kindergarten-curriculum-guide-2023', 'deped-kindergarten-policy-do-47-2016']],
    'ece-inclusive-environment' => ['medium', 'A learner who uses a mobility aid can reach the art table but cannot turn safely between crowded activity centers. What should the teacher change first?', 'Reorganize routes and materials so the learner can move among centers and choose activities.', ['Assign an adult to carry the learner to each center as needed.', 'Keep the layout and ask the learner to use only the accessible table.', 'Move the learner’s preferred activity to a separate area.'], 'Access includes movement, choice, and participation in shared activities. Adjusting the environment addresses the barrier without separating the learner from peers.', ['deped-kindergarten-curriculum-guide-2023', 'prc-let-enhanced-tos-2025']],
    'ece-play-based-learning' => ['medium', 'Children are comparing which objects roll down a ramp more slowly. How can the teacher extend the inquiry while keeping play central?', 'Ask children to predict, test one change, and describe what they notice.', ['Give the class the expected result and ask children to repeat the demonstration.', 'Replace the ramp with a worksheet so every child records the same answer.', 'Change several ramp features at once to make the activity more exciting.'], 'A focused prompt can extend prediction and observation while children continue to explore. Changing several features at once makes it harder to interpret what affected the result.', ['deped-kindergarten-curriculum-guide-2023', 'prc-let-enhanced-tos-2025']],

    'sne-accessible-materials' => ['medium', 'A learner who uses a screen reader is assigned a science activity from a scanned image-only handout. What should the teacher do before the lesson?', 'Provide an accessible, screen-reader-compatible version and check it with the learner.', ['Ask a classmate to read the handout aloud during every activity.', 'Wait until the learner requests help after the task begins.', 'Replace the science activity with a simpler unrelated worksheet.'], 'Accessible materials should be ready in time for participation and should preserve the learning purpose. Confirming usability catches reading-order or description problems that a file conversion alone may miss.', ['deped-ra11650-irr', 'republic-act-11650', 'prc-let-enhanced-tos-2025']],
    'sne-family-collaboration' => ['medium', 'A school team proposes a new participation goal but has not heard the learner’s or family’s priorities. What is the best next step?', 'Invite the learner and family to discuss priorities and combine them with school-based observations.', ['Finalize the goal first so the meeting can focus on implementing it.', 'Ask the family to choose the goal without sharing school evidence.', 'Delay the plan until the family agrees with every staff interpretation.'], 'Inclusive planning uses the learner’s and family’s knowledge alongside professional observations. Shared planning does not require ignoring evidence or waiting for perfect agreement.', ['deped-ra11650-irr', 'republic-act-11650', 'deped-ppst-do-42-2017']],
    'sne-inclusive-assessment' => ['hard', 'A class is assessing students’ ability to interpret a map legend. One learner needs the directions read aloud but can read the map symbols independently. Which approach best preserves the target skill?', 'Read the directions aloud while leaving the map and legend interpretation to the learner.', ['Read both the directions and every map symbol so the learner finishes with the group.', 'Withhold oral directions because all students must receive identical presentation.', 'Replace the map task with a verbal question about a different geography topic.'], 'The support removes an access barrier in the directions without supplying the map-reading response being assessed. Accommodations should be matched to the construct and the learner’s needs.', ['deped-ra11650-irr', 'prc-let-enhanced-tos-2025']],
    'sne-instructional-adaptation' => ['medium', 'A learner understands a science concept during discussion but cannot show the same reasoning in a dense written format. What is a sound instructional adjustment?', 'Offer an appropriate response format while keeping the concept and success criteria explicit.', ['Lower the concept objective because the written response is difficult.', 'Use the same written task and infer understanding from effort.', 'Remove assessment until the learner can complete the original format.'], 'An adaptation can change access or response mode while maintaining the intended learning outcome. The teacher should document the criteria and ensure the alternative gives valid evidence.', ['deped-ra11650-irr', 'prc-let-enhanced-tos-2025']],
    'sne-progress-monitoring' => ['medium', 'A learner’s reading goal shows little change across several weeks of comparable brief checks. What should the teacher do next?', 'Review the measures and instruction, then adjust support and continue monitoring the same goal.', ['Repeat the same instruction until the scheduled annual review.', 'Replace the goal with a broader one so small changes are easier to detect.', 'Compare the learner’s score only with the class average.'], 'Repeated, goal-aligned evidence can show whether instruction is helping. The team should check measurement quality and adjust support rather than relying on a single comparison or waiting passively.', ['deped-ra11650-irr', 'deped-ppst-do-42-2017']],
    'sne-reasonable-accommodations' => ['medium', 'A learner asks to use a familiar communication device during a class presentation. The presentation is assessing the organization of ideas. What should the teacher consider?', 'Whether the device gives access to expression without changing the organization criterion.', ['Decline the device to ensure every presentation looks the same.', 'Approve it without checking whether the device supplies or alters the target skill.', 'Replace the presentation with a participation score for the whole class.'], 'The accommodation should address the access barrier while preserving the assessed construct. A quick, individualized check can distinguish the communication method from the organization of ideas.', ['deped-ra11650-irr', 'republic-act-11650', 'prc-let-enhanced-tos-2025']],
    'sne-universal-design' => ['medium', 'A teacher plans a lesson that depends on dense projected text and a single oral explanation. Which redesign best reflects universal design?', 'Plan clear spoken and visual explanations with readable text and more than one way to engage with the task.', ['Keep the lesson unchanged and prepare an alternative only if a learner struggles.', 'Provide the same printed page to everyone and treat that as equal access.', 'Remove the challenging content so that all learners complete identical work.'], 'Planning multiple accessible ways to perceive information and participate can reduce predictable barriers for the whole class. It does not replace individualized support when needed.', ['deped-ra11650-irr', 'deped-ppst-do-42-2017']],

    'tvted-assessment-and-feedback' => ['medium', 'A trainee performs a welding setup safely but misaligns the joint. Which feedback best supports competency development?', 'Identify the alignment evidence, model the correction, and let the trainee practice again.', ['Mark the attempt incorrect and move to the next competency.', 'Praise the trainee’s effort without identifying the performance gap.', 'Complete the alignment for the trainee so the class stays on schedule.'], 'Competency feedback should connect observable performance with the standard and provide a chance to improve. Completing the task for the trainee does not establish independent competence.', ['tesda-competency-standards', 'ched-cmo-79-btvted-2017', 'prc-let-enhanced-tos-2025']],
    'tvted-competency-based-training' => ['medium', 'A trainee completes the scheduled hours for a competency but has not met the performance criteria on two required steps. What should the trainer record?', 'The trainee needs further practice and reassessment against the stated performance criteria.', ['Competency is achieved because the required attendance hours are complete.', 'The competency is achieved if the trainee can describe the steps verbally.', 'The result should be averaged with other trainees to determine achievement.'], 'Competency-based decisions are grounded in demonstrated performance against defined criteria and conditions. Attendance and peer averages do not replace individual evidence.', ['tesda-competency-standards', 'tesda-training-regulations-index', 'ched-cmo-79-btvted-2017']],
    'tvted-entrepreneurship-and-employability' => ['medium', 'A student group wants to sell a product that classmates like, but the proposed price does not cover materials and delivery. What should they examine next?', 'Revisit customer needs, costs, and the value proposition before deciding whether to revise the offer.', ['Keep the product unchanged because positive feedback proves the venture is viable.', 'Raise the price until costs are covered without checking customer willingness.', 'Drop cost analysis because the project is intended as a learning activity.'], 'A workable proposal must consider both customer value and the resources needed to deliver it. Positive interest alone does not establish economic feasibility.', ['tesda-competency-standards', 'deped-epp-tle-curriculum-guide', 'prc-let-enhanced-tos-2025']],
    'tvted-industry-alignment' => ['medium', 'A training center receives a new employer request for a software skill that is absent from the current competency unit. What is the best curriculum response?', 'Verify the skill against current occupational standards and course outcomes before revising training.', ['Add the request immediately because one employer represents the whole industry.', 'Reject the request because a published training plan should never change.', 'Replace a required competency so the schedule can remain unchanged.'], 'Industry input can reveal changing work needs, but a curriculum change should be checked against occupational standards and course outcomes. One request is evidence to investigate, not sufficient validation by itself.', ['tesda-competency-standards', 'tesda-training-regulations-index', 'ched-cmo-79-btvted-2017']],
    'tvted-introductory-vocational-teaching' => ['medium', 'After a trainer demonstrates a machine setup, most trainees can repeat it only while watching. What should happen next?', 'Use guided practice with fading prompts, then check performance without the demonstration.', ['Repeat the demonstration at the same pace until the scheduled period ends.', 'Move directly to an unfamiliar task so trainees learn through trial and error.', 'Count accurate copying as independent mastery of the setup.'], 'Guided practice can support transfer from observation to independent performance. The trainer should gather evidence after prompts are reduced.', ['ched-cmo-79-btvted-2017', 'prc-let-enhanced-tos-2025']],
    'tvted-learning-resources-and-tools' => ['medium', 'A class has one functioning tool for a task that requires each trainee to demonstrate safe setup. Which plan best protects learning and evidence quality?', 'Organize supervised rotations with a safe practice task for waiting trainees and assess each performance.', ['Let trainees share one final demonstration and infer individual competence.', 'Allow unsupervised use so that every trainee gets more machine time.', 'Replace the practical competency with a written quiz about the tool.'], 'Rotations preserve individual evidence while keeping other trainees engaged in relevant preparation. Safe supervision remains part of the competency context.', ['deped-epp-tle-curriculum-guide', 'tesda-competency-standards', 'ched-cmo-79-btvted-2017']],
    'tvted-workplace-learning' => ['medium', 'During an industry placement, a trainee is assigned repetitive tasks unrelated to the planned competency outcomes. What should the school coordinator do?', 'Consult the workplace mentor, map available tasks to outcomes, and agree on a supervised learning plan.', ['Accept the placement as valid because workplace exposure is itself the learning outcome.', 'Ask the trainee to find different work without involving the mentor.', 'End all placements because one assignment does not match the plan.'], 'A placement should connect work experience with planned competencies and supervision. Coordination can identify suitable tasks and preserve the relationship while addressing the mismatch.', ['ched-cmo-79-btvted-2017', 'tesda-competency-standards', 'prc-let-enhanced-tos-2025']],
    'tvted-workplace-safety' => ['medium', 'Before a practical session, a trainee notices a damaged power cord on the assigned equipment. What is the trainer’s best response?', 'Remove the equipment from use, report the hazard, and provide a safe alternative until it is cleared.', ['Tape the cord temporarily so the scheduled practice can proceed.', 'Ask the trainee to work carefully and report any further damage.', 'Continue with the demonstration because the trainer will operate the machine.'], 'Safety procedures begin with identifying and controlling hazards. A warning or temporary patch does not make damaged equipment safe to use.', ['tesda-competency-standards', 'deped-epp-tle-curriculum-guide', 'prc-let-enhanced-tos-2025']],

    'cae-arts-assessment' => ['medium', 'A visual-arts rubric scores color mixing even though the stated outcome is interpreting how composition guides attention. What should the teacher do?', 'Revise the criteria so evidence and feedback align with composition and interpretation.', ['Keep the rubric because color mixing is easier to score consistently.', 'Give every learner the same score to avoid disagreements about meaning.', 'Replace the outcome with color mixing after students submit their work.'], 'Assessment criteria should reflect the intended outcome. Ease of scoring is not enough if the rubric rewards a different skill.', ['deped-arts-curriculum-guide-2020', 'prc-let-enhanced-tos-2025']],
    'cae-arts-ethics-and-inclusion' => ['medium', 'A class plans a performance using a story from a local community, but no one has asked community members about its use. What is the best next step?', 'Consult appropriate community sources about permission, context, attribution, and respectful use.', ['Proceed because the story is available in a public online post.', 'Remove all community references so the performance cannot cause offense.', 'Ask the class to vote on whether permission is needed.'], 'Context and consent matter when using community knowledge. Consultation can guide attribution and appropriate use without assuming that public availability removes ethical obligations.', ['ncca-culture-arts-foundation', 'deped-arts-curriculum-guide-2020', 'prc-let-enhanced-tos-2025']],
    'cae-arts-pedagogy' => ['medium', 'Students have different levels of experience with a printmaking process, while the lesson outcome is to explain how a repeated image changes meaning. What is a sound teaching choice?', 'Provide brief process scaffolds and let students compare intentional variations in the repeated image.', ['Require identical prints before anyone may discuss meaning.', 'Focus the lesson on tool vocabulary because skill levels differ.', 'Ask experienced students to finish the prints for their group.'], 'Scaffolds can support access to the process while preserving a common interpretive outcome. Comparing intentional variations keeps the learning goal in focus.', ['deped-arts-curriculum-guide-2020', 'prc-let-enhanced-tos-2025']],
    'cae-creative-process' => ['medium', 'A student discards an early design after peer feedback changes the intended audience. How should the teacher frame the revision?', 'Ask which feedback changed the design decision and what the student wants the next version to communicate.', ['Treat the discarded draft as wasted time and grade only the final design.', 'Require the student to restore the original design for consistency.', 'Ask peers to choose the final design so the process feels collaborative.'], 'Revision is part of the creative process. A short reflection connects feedback, intention, and the student’s own next decision.', ['deped-arts-curriculum-guide-2020', 'ncca-culture-arts-foundation']],
    'cae-cultural-literacy' => ['medium', 'A student sees a visual motif in a work from a community they do not know and assigns it a universal meaning. What should the class do?', 'Seek context from reliable community or scholarly sources before interpreting the motif.', ['Keep the first interpretation because visual symbols have fixed meanings.', 'Avoid discussing cultural meaning and describe only the colors.', 'Ask one classmate from that community to speak for every member.'], 'Meaning can depend on history, practice, and the maker’s context. Research and careful attribution are better than assuming a universal reading or burdening one learner to represent a community.', ['ncca-culture-arts-foundation', 'deped-arts-curriculum-guide-2020']],
    'cae-media-and-performance' => ['medium', 'A class is choosing a medium for a short performance about an environmental issue. The venue has limited space and some audience members need captions. What should guide the choice?', 'Select a form that fits the message, venue, available resources, and audience access needs.', ['Choose the most elaborate form because technical complexity increases impact.', 'Use the first medium suggested so the class can begin rehearsing.', 'Keep the planned medium and ask audience members to adapt to it.'], 'Media and performance decisions should connect form to meaning and conditions of presentation. Access is part of audience planning, not a late add-on.', ['deped-arts-curriculum-guide-2020', 'ncca-culture-arts-foundation']],
    'cae-philippine-arts-and-heritage' => ['medium', 'A student exhibit labels a community textile as “traditional Filipino design” but gives no community, maker, or time-period information. What is the most useful correction?', 'Add verified attribution and context that identifies the source and limits of the label.', ['Keep the broad label because it is concise and celebratory.', 'Add a single national symbol so the work is easier to recognize.', 'Remove the label and display the textile without any context.'], 'Specific provenance helps learners understand diverse Philippine arts and avoids treating distinct communities and histories as interchangeable. Attribution should be verified.', ['ncca-culture-arts-foundation', 'deped-arts-curriculum-guide-2020']],
    'pe-assessment-and-inclusion' => ['medium', 'A PE assessment measures a target passing skill. One learner can demonstrate it with a lighter ball that follows the same path and decision demands. What is the fairest approach?', 'Use the access adjustment if it preserves the passing criteria, and record the conditions used.', ['Use the standard ball because a fair assessment requires identical equipment.', 'Change the passing criteria for the learner without documenting the change.', 'Replace the skill assessment with a participation score.'], 'An equipment adjustment can support access when it does not alter the target skill. The teacher should make the construct and conditions explicit so the evidence remains interpretable.', ['deped-pe-curriculum-guide', 'ched-cmo-80-bped-2017', 'prc-let-enhanced-tos-2025']],
    'pe-fitness-components' => ['medium', 'A teacher wants to assess cardiorespiratory endurance but plans to use a single maximal handgrip score. What is the main measurement problem?', 'The chosen measure does not directly represent the fitness component named in the outcome.', ['A single score is never suitable for any physical education assessment.', 'Grip strength is a measure of endurance if students are tested after exercise.', 'The outcome should be scored from attendance because it is objective.'], 'A measure should align with the stated fitness component and be used with appropriate safety and interpretation. A precise score on the wrong construct is not valid evidence for the outcome.', ['deped-pe-curriculum-guide', 'ched-cmo-80-bped-2017']],
    'pe-fitness-programming' => ['medium', 'A beginner returns to activity after a long inactive period and becomes unusually fatigued during a planned routine. What should the teacher adjust?', 'Reduce or pause the workload, check the learner’s response, and progress gradually with recovery.', ['Keep the routine unchanged so the learner adapts to the intended challenge.', 'Increase the intensity so the session ends before fatigue continues.', 'Compare the learner’s repetitions with the most active classmate.'], 'Progression should match individual response and include recovery. Unexpected fatigue is a reason to reassess workload and safety rather than to force a fixed target.', ['deped-pe-curriculum-guide', 'ched-cmo-80-bped-2017', 'prc-let-enhanced-tos-2025']],
    'pe-movement-literacy' => ['medium', 'A learner can throw toward a target but repeatedly steps across the line before releasing the ball. Which feedback is most useful for the next practice?', 'Give one clear cue about the step and let the learner try again while observing the movement.', ['Give several corrections at once so the full movement changes immediately.', 'Stop the learner from throwing until the movement is identical to a model.', 'Score the throw only by distance and ignore the movement pattern.'], 'A focused cue directs attention to an observable part of the movement and leaves room for practice. Multiple simultaneous instructions can make it difficult to use feedback.', ['deped-pe-curriculum-guide', 'prc-let-enhanced-tos-2025']],
    'pe-physical-activity-safety' => ['easy', 'Before a class game, the teacher notices a loose floor panel in the playing area. What should happen first?', 'Keep learners away from the hazard, report it, and use a safe area or activity until it is addressed.', ['Mark the panel with a cone and continue the same game around it.', 'Ask learners to avoid the panel while the teacher supervises the game.', 'Shorten the game so exposure to the hazard is reduced.'], 'The hazard should be controlled before activity proceeds. A marker or reminder does not remove the risk created by a loose surface.', ['deped-pe-curriculum-guide', 'ched-cmo-80-bped-2017']],
    'pe-rhythm-and-dance' => ['medium', 'A group loses the beat when learning a dance phrase with several direction changes. What is a helpful teaching progression?', 'Practice the rhythm and phrase in shorter parts, then combine them with the direction changes.', ['Repeat the full phrase faster so learners become accustomed to its timing.', 'Remove the rhythm so learners can focus only on directions.', 'Ask the most coordinated learner to lead while others copy continuously.'], 'Breaking a phrase into manageable parts supports timing and coordination before integration. The teacher can then check whether learners can combine the elements.', ['deped-pe-curriculum-guide', 'ched-cmo-80-bped-2017']],
    'pe-sports-skills-and-tactics' => ['medium', 'A team passes accurately in drills but bunches around the ball during a small-sided game. Which practice best addresses the tactical problem?', 'Use a small-sided task that rewards creating and using space, then discuss the choices made.', ['Increase passing distance so players have to move faster.', 'Repeat isolated passing drills until every pass is accurate.', 'Assign fixed positions before learners understand the space problem.'], 'The issue appears during decision-making and spatial support, not basic passing accuracy alone. A constrained game makes the tactical demand visible and gives learners evidence to discuss.', ['deped-pe-curriculum-guide', 'prc-let-enhanced-tos-2025']],
];
